# Independent audit verifier (launch gate 5)

You are the independent verifier. You did not write this code.

## Hard prohibitions

- Never fix app code
- Never merge
- Never push to main
- Never write to production data (live Supabase project `hvwakffluwvegedefoth`)
- Never change migrations, Edge Functions, RLS, or sibling backend from this pass

## Repos

- `shahafrach/haimunia-club` (club app, live https://haimunia.pages.dev)
- `shahafrach/haimunia-app-demo` (shared Supabase backend) — local stack only
- `haimuniya/haimunia-app` (old app, read only)

## Branch and findings

- Work on branch `audit/final` in haimunia-club
- Record every issue in `FINDINGS.md`: ID, severity, app, location, steps, expected vs actual, suggested fix, status=open
- Cite STANDARD.md codes
- Severity: critical (blocks launch), high, medium, low
- Also run every check in `docs/audit/CURSOR-CHECKS.md`

## Scope checklist

1. Database (local): RLS, SECURITY DEFINER, grants, `supabase test db`, advisors; focus delete_my_account, request_account_deletion, feedback_submit, client_error_report, transfer_put limits, F-005 policies
2. Live site security: headers/CSP on haimunia.pages.dev and box-log.pages.dev; non-public paths 404; gitleaks; npm audit
3. Member flows live and local, Chromium and WebKit, 390x844 / 360x780 / 1440x900
4. Data safety: synthetic 3-year fixture backup+transfer hashes; upgrade 3.7.2 and 3.12.0 → 3.17.1
5. Offline and SW update during save
6. a11y/RTL: axe zero serious/critical; keyboard; 200% zoom; contrast; Hebrew formats
7. Code review since 3.8.0: src/db.js, sw.js, update path in app.js, src/transfer.js — data-loss paths

## Budget

- Run only what each step needs
- One full `npm test` in the foreground at the end
- No background watchers, sleep loops or polling
- Do not re-run a suite that passed

## Deliverable

- Push `audit/final`
- Final report in English, short, one block per step: pass/fail, findings by severity with IDs, what could not be checked and why
- Last line: `Launch blockers: yes or no`
